  <p>If you go to Kyoto with kids, my honest advice is to pick fewer things and go slower. We tried to fit too much into that first day and it broke us. The second day worked because we let Uji be the whole day. The rest of the time we just walked, sat in shrines, and ate small meals. That part of Kyoto, the slow part, is the part we'll actually remember.</p>
